# 2. Flip-Flops — JK, D and T

Flip-flops are clock-controlled sequential storage elements used extensively in digital systems.

## JK Flip-Flop

| J | K | Next State |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | 0 | Hold |
| 0 | 1 | Reset |
| 1 | 0 | Set |
| 1 | 1 | Toggle |

### Key Point

JK Flip-Flop removes the invalid input combination of the basic SR Flip-Flop and provides a **toggle** operation.

🔗 [JK Flip-Flop — RTL + Testbench + Simulation](https://www.edaplayground.com/x/DWxZ)

---

## D Flip-Flop

| D | Next Q |
|---|---|
| 0 | 0 |
| 1 | 1 |

A D Flip-Flop transfers the input **D to Q at the active clock edge**.

### Typical Use

- Data storage
- Registers
- Pipelining

🔗 [D Flip-Flop — RTL + Testbench + Simulation](https://www.edaplayground.com/x/M2mX)

---

## T Flip-Flop

| T | Next State |
|---|---|
| 0 | Hold |
| 1 | Toggle |

### Typical Use

- Counters
- Frequency division
- Sequential control circuits

